<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heinrich von Kleist</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1777–1811</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Heinrich von Kleist was a German dramatist, poet and short-story writer from a Prussian military family. His plays include the comedy The Broken Jug, Penthesilea and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-prince-of-homburg">The Prince of Homburg</a>, and his novellas include Michael Kohlhaas and The Marquise of O. Little recognised in his lifetime, he took his own life near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> in 1811 and is now ranked among the greatest German writers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heinrich-von-kleist.jpg" alt="Heinrich von Kleist" width="320" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anton Graff · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anton_Graff_Heinrich_von_Kleist_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
